                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "220aee42-0ce4-4c2d-841b-9de1afa08007",
                                "sense_id": "068f238a-82c6-37c1-91fb-8a3f8b1edb25",
                                "text": "their coition is made by supersaliency, like that of horses, as we are informed by some who have beheld them in that act"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "848353d5-aecc-4c30-b36f-e8dbcd6f9195",
                                "sense_id": "068f238a-82c6-37c1-91fb-8a3f8b1edb25",
                                "text": "A mare put to a stallion fell dead at the end of coition."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc581c21-ab68-4fdc-bec5-6415c729a429",
                                "sense_id": "068f238a-82c6-37c1-91fb-8a3f8b1edb25",
                                "text": "Sex without the consummating act of coition is never quite sex, in human relationships: just as a eunuch is never quite a man."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3858f1e3-bb13-4340-a83e-f2586d625611",
                                "sense_id": "068f238a-82c6-37c1-91fb-8a3f8b1edb25",
                                "text": "All sages and physicians agree in saying that the ills which afflict man originate with the abuse of coition."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
